|CKBBard|000

|CK0Bards are flexible performers who mix combat, support, control, scouting,
and social manipulation. They trade narrow specialization for a broad toolkit
that can keep a party moving or adapt when a fight changes shape.|000

|CKBHow it plays|000
|CK0Songs build Performance, especially when the Bard varies rhythm, melody,
harmony, dissonance, crescendo, and finale forms. Many songs create fields that
follow the Bard and pulse over nearby allies or enemies. Charisma strengthens
those performances, while instruments and a later archetype choice reshape the
songbook.|000

|CKBCore skills|000
|CK0pulsebeat builds momentum, soothe and rally support allies, dirgeash and
wail pressure enemies, and battlefieldsilence disrupts hostile casting.
Perform, fame, defame, lore, and study give the guild useful tools away from
direct combat.|000

|CKBBest fit|000
|CK0Choose Bard if you enjoy rotating abilities, reacting to the room, helping
a group, and discovering combinations instead of repeating one attack. Bards
can use broad equipment, though heavy gear interferes with subtler techniques.|000

|CK0After joining, use |CKBbardhelp general|CK0, |CKBbardhelp songs|CK0, and
|CKBbardhelp archetypes|CK0 for the full guide.|000

